# No CSS `zoom` for responsive scaling

Safari and Chrome implement the CSS `zoom` property differently. Safari
double-scales inherited font sizes inside a zoomed subtree, so any component
that sizes its text with `em` units explodes on iPhone/iPad while looking
perfect in Chrome and in Chromium-based device emulation.

This actually happened: the hero offer group (`.ob-group` — badge image +
`.pb-container` price disc) was shrunk on mobile with
`@media { .ob-group { zoom: 0.5 } }`. Chrome rendered it correctly; iOS Safari
blew the "Retail $540 / $99 / PER PACKAGE" text up ~2.5× (1/zoom) while the
circle stayed the right size.

## The fix pattern

Give each element its final on-screen size per breakpoint — the same mechanism
the working `.rd-badge-wrap .pb-container` discs use:

```css
/* ❌ BAD — scale a group with zoom */
@media (max-width: 767px) { .ob-group { zoom: 0.5; } }

/* ✅ GOOD — explicit final sizes; em-based internals scale from font-size */
@media (max-width: 767px) {
  .ob-combo .pb-container { font-size: 8px; }   /* disc = 19.4em */
  .ob-sticker img { width: 390px; }
}
```

Notes:

- `body { zoom: 0.9 }` at ≥992px still exists in these sites (desktop-only,
  legacy Webflow parity). Don't add new dependencies on it, and don't copy the
  pattern to new components.
- Offsets tuned "pre-zoom" (e.g. `translateX(58px)` inside zoom 0.4) must be
  converted to on-screen values (23px) when removing zoom.
- Chromium emulation will NOT catch this bug. Verify hero/mobile layouts in
  the iOS Simulator: `xcrun simctl openurl booted <url>`.
